---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import DocShell from "../../components/DocShell.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../../components/CommandBlock.astro";
---

<Layout title="Review Workflow | ArkheionX Docs" description="A practical local ArkheionX workflow for Solidity and Foundry review.">
  <DocShell>
    <p class="page-kicker">Use</p>
    <h1>Review workflow.</h1>
    <p class="doc-deck">Use ArkheionX to preserve orientation and evidence state while keeping source reading and judgment in the foreground.</p>

    <h2>1. Pin the working state</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`git status --short
git rev-parse HEAD
arkheionx version`} />
    <p>Record the exact repository commit and tool version before comparing artifacts across reviewers or time.</p>

    <h2>2. Establish orientation</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx doctor .
arkheionx open .
arkheionx map .
arkheionx flow .`} />
    <p>Read the source alongside the output. Correct any mental model that conflicts with implementation; the generated labels are provisional.</p>

    <h2>3. Build the review map</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx review-map .
arkheionx value-paths . --top 10
arkheionx assumptions . --top 10
arkheionx test-gap-map . --top 10`} />
    <p>Use the focused views to form a review queue. Trace authority and value paths before spending time on isolated low-context signals.</p>

    <h2>4. Attach evidence</h2>
    <p>
      Evidence commands can reuse generated proof, trace, and local validation artifacts. Execution remains optional
      and explicit. Review project test configuration before enabling <code>--run</code> or <code>--build</code>.
    </p>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx proof-plan .
arkheionx evidence-status .
arkheionx evidence-links .
arkheionx validate-artifacts .`} />

    <h2>5. Build a handoff package</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx review-package . --strict
find .arkheionx/out/review-package -maxdepth 2 -type f -print`} />
    <p>Inspect the manifest, checksums, validation result, and copied artifacts. Remove sensitive or out-of-scope material before sharing.</p>

    <h2>6. Write conclusions separately</h2>
    <p>
      Keep the human conclusion distinct from generated context. Document source references, impact reasoning,
      preconditions, contradictory evidence, and confidence. Final severity belongs to the review process, not the
      artifact generator.
    </p>
  </DocShell>
</Layout>
